# Internal working notes (not part of the published workflow)
CLAUDE.md
# Claude Code skills: same category -- guidance for an assistant driving this
# repo, not part of the CLI workflow. RUNBOOK.md is the human-facing copy.
.claude/skills/

# Per-system inputs and run output. `systems/*/system.ini` IS published -- it is
# the whole configuration of a system, and the only per-system file `rbfe`
# reads. Everything beside it is regenerable: inputs come from `rbfe-prep`,
# hybrid/ from `rbfe hybrid`, complex/ and solvent/ from `rbfe build`+`rbfe
# inputs`, and the rest is simulation output.
systems/*/inputs/
systems/*/hybrid/
systems/*/complex/
systems/*/solvent/
systems/*/fep.tcl

# 4YLJ -- the second worked system, deliberately not published. Its builder
# diverged from the 6I5I workflow by 632 lines and `rbfe/` is the generalized
# replacement for both; neither README nor the Chinese guide mentions it.
4YLJ/

# `rbfe verify` scratch
/tmp-verify*/
